-- Reviewed by hand (Task 6). This is the only converted file with real conversion
-- defects. It is an INACTIVE variation (conf/windowrule.conf points at
-- windowrules/default.conf, which is comment-only), so nothing below is live.
--
-- Four defect classes, all visible against conf/windowrules/default52.conf:
--
-- 1. SELECTOR PREFIX SWALLOWED (5 rules, lines 9/16/23/30/38 below). The hyprlang
--    form `windowrule = float, title:^(pavucontrol)$` selects on TITLE. The converter
--    emitted `match = { class = "title:^(pavucontrol)$" }` -- the `title:` prefix is
--    kept inside the class VALUE instead of choosing the match field. Correct form is
--    `match = { title = "^(pavucontrol)$" }`. Every one of these 5 rules matches
--    nothing as written.
--
-- 2. RULES MERGED, so counts are not 1:1. Source lines 11/12/13 are three separate
--    `windowrule` directives for Picture-in-Picture; they became ONE hl.window_rule
--    with float+pin+move. Source lines 28/29/30 are three `layerrule` directives; they
--    became ONE hl.layer_rule. Result: 9 hyprlang window rules -> 7 hl.window_rule
--    calls, 3 layer rules -> 1 hl.layer_rule call. If this variation is ever activated,
--    hypr-config-audit will read that as MISSING 2 / MISSING 2 -- a merge artefact, not
--    a dropped rule. It would need a MAPPING_DELTA entry, not a "fix".
--
-- 3. THREE ACTIONS DROPPED outright, each left as a TODO below and each counted in the
--    converter's own report (flagged=4, coverage=75.0%, exit 3):
--      source :16  `idleinhibit fullscreen`  -- rule emitted with NO action at all
--      source :21  `xwayland:1`              -- selector dropped
--      source :30  `ignorezero`              -- layer rule dropped
--
-- 4. DANGEROUS: the rule from source :21 lost BOTH its selectors (`class:^(\bresolve\b)$`
--    and `xwayland:1`) but KEPT `no_blur = true`. A window rule with an empty match
--    applies to EVERY window, so activating this file as-is would disable blur globally.
--
-- Left unfixed deliberately: this is inactive upstream ML4W content, it cannot be
-- tested without flipping the variation, and guessing at the intended selectors would
-- be worse than the loud failure the TODO markers guarantee.
-- =====================================================================================

hl.window_rule({
    match = {
        class = "title:^(pavucontrol)$",
    },
    float = true,
})

hl.window_rule({
    match = {
        class = "title:^(blueman-manager)$",
    },
    float = true,
})

hl.window_rule({
    match = {
        class = "title:^(nm-connection-editor)$",
    },
    float = true,
})

hl.window_rule({
    match = {
        class = "title:^(qalculate-gtk)$",
    },
    float = true,
})

-- Browser Picture in Picture
hl.window_rule({
    match = {
        class = "title:^(Picture-in-Picture)$",
    },
    float = true,
    pin = true,
    move = "69.5% 4%",
})

-- idleinhibit
hl.window_rule({
    match = {
        class = "class:([window])",
    },
    -- TODO: manual review — unmapped window rule action: "idleinhibit fullscreen"
})

--xwayland related rules
-- when moving objects in resolve a large border is produced 
-- This rule prevents that and serves as a template for any problematic xwayland apps
hl.window_rule({
    no_blur = true,
    -- TODO: manual review — unmapped window rule action: "class:^(\\bresolve\\b)$"
    -- TODO: manual review — unmapped window rule action: "xwayland:1"
})

-- This is a general rule for xwayland apps but can have other consequences 
-- for one user it impacted EMACs so it's disabled by default 
-- It's here as a reference or for quick triage of xwayland ap
--windowrule = noblur, xwayland:1

-- Waybar blur
hl.layer_rule({
    match = { namespace = "waybar" },
    blur = true,
    ignore_alpha = 0.01,
    -- TODO: manual review — unmapped layer rule: "ignorezero"
})

